Tailscale is a VPN-based networking tool that creates a secure private network between your devices.

On the first machine, you sign in to Tailscale using a Google account.
On the second machine, you log in using the same Google account.

Since both machines are authenticated under the same account, they become part of the same tailnet.

A tailnet is the private network created by Tailscale. It is not just a network interface, but a secure overlay network managed by Tailscale.

After logging in, both machines will appear in the Tailscale admin dashboard. Each device is automatically assigned a private IP address (usually in the range 100.x.x.x).

Using this private IP address, you can securely connect from one machine to another (for example, using RDP, SSH, etc.).

